# Verify {{ project_name }}

Use `./gradlew` on macOS/Linux and `gradlew.bat` on Windows.

```shell
./gradlew spotlessApply
./gradlew build
```

`build` compiles with Error Prone and NullAway, runs `spotlessCheck` and the test suite.
{%- if profile == "backend" %} Integration tests are skipped when Docker is unavailable; say so in your report instead of claiming they passed.{% endif %}

On failure: read the first error in the output, fix issues introduced by the current change, and rerun `./gradlew build`. For a single test: `./gradlew test --tests '*ClassName'`.

Report pre-existing or environment-related failures separately instead of working around them (no `@SuppressWarnings`, `@Disabled` or excluded checks without the user's agreement).
